cff-version: 1.2.0
title: TransitionListener
message: >-
  If you use TransitionListener in your work, please cite the v2.0 release
  paper and the v1 release paper that introduced the framework.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Carlo
    family-names: Tasillo
    email: carlo.tasillo@ific.uv.es
    affiliation: IFIC Valencia
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2683-5169"
  - given-names: Jonas
    family-names: Matuszak
    email: jonas.matuszak@kit.edu
    affiliation: Karlsruhe Institute of Technology
repository-code: "https://github.com/tasicarl/TransitionListener"
url: "https://tasillo.de/TransitionListener/"
abstract: >-
  TransitionListener is an open-source Python framework for analyzing
  cosmological first-order phase transitions and their stochastic
  gravitational-wave backgrounds. It implements a full thermal history
  from microphysical model parameters to observable signals, including a
  precision percolation solver, the LTE bubble-wall velocity, and
  state-of-the-art gravitational-wave spectra.
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - gravitational waves
  - phase transitions
  - particle physics
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: 2026-04-26
